-- title:
--   Cuspidal mod p modular functions lift to cusp forms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, let $N \ge 1$ be an integer with $p \nmid N$, let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and let $m$ be a natural number. Inside the field of Laurent series `LaurentSeries K` put $\bar\jmath =$ `jqModC K`, the series $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $K$ of the integral power series `jNum`, and let $\bar\jmath_N =$ `jqNModC K N` be its image under `qExpand K N`; `modularFunctionFieldC K N` is the intermediate field $K(\bar\jmath, \bar\jmath_N)$ of `LaurentSeries K`. Let $G$ be an element of this field satisfying `IsModPCuspFormFn K m`, i.e. (i) $G^{6}\,\bar\jmath^{\,4m}\,(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3m}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath$, and (ii) for some natural number $M$ the element $G^{2M}\,\bar\jmath^{\,mM+1}\,(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{mM}$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\bar\jmath^{-1}$. The conclusion is that there is a power series $\varphi \in K[[q]]$ lying in [`ModPForms.modPCusp N (2 * (m : ℤ)) K`](def/CuspForm_ModPForms.html#L7) — the $K$-span of those power series $\sum_n (a_n \bmod p)\,q^n$ arising from an integer sequence $(a_n)$ that is the sequence of $q$-expansion coefficients of some cusp form of weight $2m$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ — whose image in `LaurentSeries K` equals `qexpOfWeight K (m : ℤ) G`, that is $G \cdot (\theta\bar\jmath)^{m}$ with $\theta\bar\jmath =$ `thetaJ K`.
--
--   This is the cuspidal companion of the Katz–Serre style lifting statement: a weight-$2m$ mod $p$ modular function on $X_0(N)$ whose integrality conditions express vanishing at the cusps has its $q$-expansion in the mod $p$ cuspidal space. It is used in the construction of Hecke eigenforms in the supersingular/Riemann–Roch part of the development, where the cuspidal space at a dual weight is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModPForms_exists_mem_modPCusp_ofPowerSeries_eq_qexpOfWeight_of_isModPCuspFormFn.lean

